Here is the finding. The fault sits on the search→rate path, not in `rate`'s own process. I'm naming `search` as the faulty service with `dns_lookup_failed`. Hubble network metrics are absent, so I can't confirm a network-level kind, and I'm choosing DNS because the failed calls return in about 0.01 ms with no connection attempt. The `geo` memory jump (~22 MB → ~1 GB) has no latency or error effect on its callers, so it stays inside `geo` and isn't counted.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "dns_lookup_failed",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT attr_status_code, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,3) med_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,3) p95_ms, count(DISTINCT trace_id) traces FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "361 of 364 search→rate.GetRates client spans are Error with median ~0.013 ms; they fail before any connection."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='rate' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='rate' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "rate server spans fall from 1065 in normal period to 1 in abnormal; rate receives almost no calls from search."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, min(value) mn, max(value) mx, count(*) n FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE service_name='rate' AND metric='k8s.pod.uptime' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "rate pod uptime climbs continuously with no reset, so rate did not restart and its pod stayed up."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT attr_status_code, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "search Nearby server spans are 361 Error versus 3 Unset in the abnormal window; normal is all Unset."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND (span_name='search.Search/Nearby' OR span_name='HTTP /hotels') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "frontend's search.Search/Nearby client calls and HTTP /hotels server spans are all Error (301); normal /hotels was 200 OK."}]}
  ]
}
```

